      <h2>Why Coastal Crosby Needs a Specialist</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Crosby is one of the most affluent parts of north Merseyside. The L23 average property price sits around £436,000. Blundellsands seafront homes change hands at £1 million to £2 million. The 1930s semis in the wider area average £313,000.</p>

        <p>What makes Crosby different from inland Liverpool is the salt air. Properties on Hall Road, Mariners Road, Burbo Bank Road South and the wider seafront are within a few hundred metres of the Irish Sea. External boiler flues, condensate pipes, outside taps and any exposed copper pipework corrode noticeably faster than inland equivalents.</p>

        <p>A boiler flue that would last 15 years inland might need replacement at 10 in coastal Crosby. A compromised flue is a carbon monoxide risk. We check flue integrity as standard on every coastal property service. If you notice rust streaks below your flue terminal, call us straight away.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>The larger Blundellsands and St Andrews Road detached homes have substantial heating and hot water systems. Five bathrooms. Two or three heating zones. Premium fixtures from Hansgrohe, Grohe and Villeroy & Boch. A diagnostic call-out here needs the right kit and the right experience.</p>

        <p>We work in Crosby every week. We carry G3 qualifications for unvented cylinder work and premium brand spares. We also handle the apartment blocks along the seafront, the period terraces in Crosby Village and the stone-built cottages in Little Crosby. One number for all of it.</p>
