      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£80 an hour weekdays 9am to 5pm. £120 an hour weekends 9am to 1pm. £150 an hour out of hours, nights and bank holidays. 1 hour minimum on every call-out. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost £80 to £350 total. Written quote before work starts. No separate call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>30 minute response guaranteed across Crosby L23. We dispatch from Kirkby. Typical arrival is 20 to 25 minutes via the A5036 or M57. A real person answers the phone any time of day or night.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">COASTAL</span>&nbsp; Does being near the sea cause more plumbing problems in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Coastal properties in Crosby experience faster corrosion on external pipework, boiler flues, condensate pipes and outside tap fittings. Salt air and increased moisture accelerate the rusting process. Properties close to Crosby Beach on Hall Road, Mariners Road and Burbo Bank Road South are worst affected. If you notice rust staining on an external flue terminal, call us straight away. A compromised flue is a carbon monoxide risk.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BLUNDELLSANDS</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Blundellsands seafront properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The large detached homes on Warren Road, St Andrews Road, Anthonys Road and The Serpentine are familiar work. These often have multiple bathrooms, unvented mains pressure cylinders, underfloor heating and premium fixtures. We're G3 qualified for unvented cylinder work and carry common spares for premium brands.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">APARTMENTS</span>&nbsp; Do you work on Crosby's coastal apartment blocks?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Burbo Mansions, Gaywood Court, Fountain Court and the wider apartment stock around the seafront have communal water and heating systems. We coordinate with managing agents where access is needed to risers or pump rooms. Same fixed rates for apartment work.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">PERIOD</span>&nbsp; Can you handle period property plumbing in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Crosby's Victorian and Edwardian properties date from the 1850s onwards. Original lead pipework and cast iron column radiators are still in service in places. We carry replacement parts and work around original features. The 1850s stone-built cottages in Little Crosby village need particular care which we provide as standard.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All our engineers are Gas Safe registered. It's illegal to carry out gas work without this qualification. Verify our registration at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We provide gas safety certificates for all gas work carried out.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
